      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors concluded that a large stump of the gall-bladder duct is of no independent importance as a cause of the affection. However, concretions may be formed in the stump, that was evident in three cases, therefore, the gall duct stump should be no more than 0.5 cm."},
